  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of Direct Protection Assistance and GBV Response Services to Affected Populations in Oromia and Somalia Regions of Ethiopia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Internally displaced persons (IDPs) in Ethiopia predominantly live in collective sites which lack dignified and safe living conditions, insufficient access to basic services and lack of necessary resources to sustain their families and communities. There are also numerous protection concerns as a direct result of these conditions, including negative coping mechanisms in response to dire living conditions and unprincipled returns/relocations, which often disregard participation from IDPs, an important element for informed, safe and dignified returns. The overall goal of this project is to strengthen the provision of direct protection assistance, including gender-based violence (GBV) response services to IDPs and IDP returnees in Oromia (East Hararge) and Somalia regions (Fafan). The interventions will be in line with IOM&#x2019;s Institutional Framework for Addressing GBV in crises and IOM&#x2019;s protection policy.</narrative>
  </description>
